A better question is: **Which activities require the same scarce resource, which activities must wait for a readiness or clearance condition rather than merely a preceding clock time, and which activities must start or finish together to meet the doors, program, reception and venue-reset milestones?** Applied here, the AV check must finish before the rehearsal can use the stage; the foyer setup, registration setup and FOH walkthrough must be ready before doors; doors must wait for the walkthrough; ushering must wait for registration to close; the host must wait for the hall to be seated; the keynote deck, product video and stage appearances must be sequenced through the single projector and stage; reception service must begin when the host closes; registration breakdown must wait until guests have left the hall; and the stage strike must wait until the hall is clear. No cooling, resting, thawing, proofing or holding step is implied. I added only an inferred zero-duration hall-clear confirmation gate because the text requires breakdown and strike to wait for that condition. The requested validation, schedule analysis and visualization tools are unavailable in this session, so no live URL or tool-generated Gantt can be supplied.

